  beschreibung: Mars is a cold, dry desert world with a very thin atmosphere. Its
    red color comes from oxidized iron minerals in its dust and rock. Mars has enormous
    landforms such as the volcano Olympus Mons and the canyon system Valles Marineris.
    Traces of ancient rivers and lakes make it important for the question of whether
    habitable conditions once existed there.
  planetSizeInfoText: Mars is much smaller than Earth. Its diameter is a little more
    than half of Earth's diameter.
  orbitalDistanceInfoText: Mars orbits the Sun at about 1.52 AU, outside Earth's
    orbit.
  orbitalSpeedInfoText: A Martian year lasts about 687 Earth days. Because of its
    greater distance, Mars moves around the Sun more slowly than Earth.
  axialTiltInfoText: Mars' axial tilt is similar to Earth's, so Mars also has seasons.
  eccentricityInfoText: Mars' orbit is noticeably elliptical, so its closest and
    farthest points from the Sun differ more than Earth's.
  planetScaleInfoText: In a size comparison, Mars is about half as wide as Earth,
    but much smaller in volume.
  gravityInfoText: Gravity is about 38 percent of Earth's gravity. Movements would
    feel lighter and more jump-like.
  fakten:
  - Mars looks red because iron in its rocks and dust has oxidized, similar to rust.
  - Valles Marineris is a huge canyon system and one of the largest canyons in the solar system.
  - Mars has polar ice caps, dust storms, ancient volcanoes, and many impact craters.
